#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""octo-feather-gate: the gate's two tiers.

Which tier runs and when (checkpoints, provisional heads, the shared-machinery list):
issue-lifecycle #lanes-checkpoints. What the fast tier runs: quality #recipe-fast.

  octo-feather-gate checkpoint START [--full] [--no-fast]
      In a lane worktree whose HEAD is the candidate head integrated onto START: the tier, `full` or
      `fast`, on line 1, why on line 2. --no-fast: the repo has no fast recipe. Paths are matched by
      git (rename detection for the reason shown).
  octo-feather-gate record --reason R --seconds S
      Records HEAD's full pass as a git note under refs/notes/octo-feather-gate, JSON: tier, head,
      branch, clean (the tree after the gate), gate_config (sha256 over each configuration file's
      verified blob id, `absent` for a missing one), list (the list file's blob id, or `absent`),
      reason, seconds, at. A git note, not a state dir file: it sits on the commit it proves, every
      worktree of the repo reads it, and it does not depend on the Herdr session that ran the gate.
  octo-feather-gate passed [REV]
      Prints REV's (default HEAD) recorded full pass and exits 0, else exits 1.
  octo-feather-gate config [REV]
      Prints REV's (default HEAD) identity fields as record writes them, JSON: gate_config, list;
      merge-ask reads it (when a pass is current: issue-lifecycle #lanes-checkpoints).
  octo-feather-gate select
      In the kit: the fast tier's pytest node ids for `just check-tests`, one per line; each item
      with why it runs, or why not, on stderr. Test items: each tests/*.sh (its test_gate.py
      item), and each pytest test function outside test_gate.py, named by its node id, as pytest
      collects them (tests/gate/kit/). The selection reads the coverage map (below) and the list;
      an item without recorded coverage always runs; a tests/*.sh whose own header has the line
      `# gate: e2e`, or a pytest item carrying pytest's e2e marker, is end-to-end. A pytest item's
      file is the file its node id names. Changed files count from the diff
      base, the newer of the map head and the latest commit of HEAD's history with a recorded full
      pass on a clean tree (record); a test item changed since the map head always runs. A changed
      file no recorded coverage reaches that the list names, or that is absent at the map head (the
      map cannot know it), runs every non-e2e item.
  octo-feather-gate changed
      The test items the change adds or changes, one pytest argument per line: a tests/*.sh as its
      test_gate.py node id, any other changed file as its path (a pytest item's file); test_gate.py
      itself is no item's; a test file (test_*.py) that directly imports a changed in-repo file
      is named too (one level, by ast: a kit scenario NAME.py names test_NAME.py; imports are
      resolved from the dirs holding test files or a conftest.py, never the configured
      pythonpath, scripts/). Its misses: a file reached only through another import (testkit, as
      a scenario imports it), and what a test runs by path, never imports: tests/lib/*
      (prepared.py, its .sh helpers), fixtures, a tests/*.sh item's helpers. Changed: differing
      from the merge base of HEAD with the default branch, to the working tree, untracked files
      too: the change's net changes, so a file changed and restored is none, the same on CI (a
      checkout with the default branch's history). The default branch from local refs, no
      network: origin/HEAD; else origin/<name>, then the local <name>, for init.defaultBranch,
      main, master. None found: none judged. Where from on stderr. Not select's diff base, which
      is for selection. The gate's per-test CPU budget reads it (tests/gate/conftest.py; quality
      #acceptance-test-cpu-budget).
  octo-feather-gate map DATA_DIR --junit FILE
      In the kit, under its uv venv (coverage): writes the coverage map from a mapping run's data
      (just fast-map), one coverage data dir per gate item, DATA_DIR/<item>/ (<item> GATE_ITEM: a
      tests/*.sh path, or a pytest node id, its `/` and `::` kept); files measured under
      /tmp copies of the kit map back to tracked files by their longest shared path suffix. FILE is
      the run's pytest junit xml: only an item it reports passed is mapped; a failed or skipped one
      is left out and named in the map as not passed. An item with no data (not run, or no Python
      measured) is left out of the map too.
  octo-feather-gate untouched save FILE [--mise-state DIR] [--run-tmp TMP]
  octo-feather-gate untouched check FILE
      A gate run leaves the caller's mise state and its repo's git config as it found them (owner
      ruling #584, #587; #664), judged only on what this run left, attributed exactly, so another
      agent's work on the box meanwhile never fails it. save, before the run, writes into FILE the
      content of DIR's tracked-configs and trusted-configs (each entry a link's target, a file's
      sha256), the current repo's git common dir config (every worktree's) as key/value pairs
      (`git config --file F --list`), and TMP, the run's own TMPDIR (its name the run's id).
      check, after it, fails (exit 1) naming each: an entry added, removed or changed whose link
      target, saved or new, lies under TMP, or under a dir of the git common dir's octo-feather/
      whose name carries the run's id; a config key/value added or removed, branch.<name>.* aside
      (push -u, worktree branches). Every other entry change, dangling or not (a peer lane's
      post-merge prune meanwhile), is printed as not this run's, never a failure. Else one line
      naming what it found unchanged. Content, never mtimes. DIR empty (no mise): the config
      alone; outside a git repo, the mise state alone. just check-tests runs both around every
      outermost gate run, which it gives its own TMP.
  octo-feather-gate base
      HEAD's merge base with the default branch, as changed finds it (the same code): `<sha> <ref>`
      on stdout, exit 0; none found (no HEAD, no default branch, no merge base), says so on stderr
      and exits 1. For a check that judges a change against the default branch
      (scripts/check-fake-gh).

The list is the repo root's shared-machinery.txt: one git pathspec per line, glob magic, `#`
comment lines; git itself matches it. Maps live in the repo's git common dir,
octo-feather/fast-map/<head>.json, shared by every worktree. select and map are kit-only: the
kit's tests run the kit's scripts as commands (shell items, and pytest items that run their
scenario as a command), which no stack's test impact tool maps; a target uses its stack's own
tool. Stdlib only, but map, which reads coverage data.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import ast
import datetime as dt
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from collections import Counter
from pathlib import Path
from typing import TypedDict, cast

LIST = "shared-machinery.txt"
NOTES = "refs/notes/octo-feather-gate"
CONFIG = (
    "justfile",
    "Justfile",
    ".justfile",
    "mise.toml",
    "mise.lock",
    "uv.lock",
    "pnpm-lock.yaml",
)
NODE = "tests/gate/test_gate.py::"
E2E = "# gate: e2e"


def git(*args: str, check: bool = True) -> str:
    r = subprocess.run(["git", *args], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)  # noqa: S607
    if check and r.returncode:
        sys.exit(f"octo-feather-gate: git {' '.join(args)}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return r.stdout


def ok(*args: str) -> bool:
    return subprocess.run(["git", *args], capture_output=True, check=False).returncode == 0  # noqa: S607


def lines(text: str) -> list[str]:
    return [s for s in (x.strip() for x in text.splitlines()) if s and not s.startswith("#")]


def entries(rev: str) -> list[str]:
    return lines(git("show", f"{rev}:{LIST}", check=False))


def specs(pats: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    return [f":(glob){p}" for p in dict.fromkeys(pats)]


def records() -> list[dict[str, object]]:
    out: list[dict[str, object]] = []
    for row in git("notes", f"--ref={NOTES}", "list", check=False).splitlines():
        note = row.split()[0]
        try:
            rec = json.loads(git("cat-file", "blob", note))
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if isinstance(rec, dict):
            out.append(rec)  # pyright: ignore[reportUnknownArgumentType]
    return out


def pilot_pass(start: str, branch: str) -> str | None:
    """The latest full pass recorded on BRANCH at START or an ancestor (fewest commits back)."""
    best: tuple[int, str] | None = None
    for rec in records():
        head = rec.get("head")
        if rec.get("branch") != branch or not isinstance(head, str):
            continue
        if ok("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", head, start):
            n = int(git("rev-list", "--count", f"{head}..{start}"))
            best = min(best or (n, head), (n, head))
    return best[1] if best else None


def checkpoint(start: str, *, full: bool, fast: bool) -> tuple[str, str]:
    why: list[str] = []
    if full:
        why.append("forced (--full)")
    if not fast:
        why.append("no fast recipe in this repo: its one gate is the full tier")
    branch = git("symbolic-ref", "-q", "--short", "HEAD", check=False).strip() or "HEAD"
    passed = pilot_pass(start, branch)
    if passed is None:
        why.append(f"pilot: no full pass recorded on {branch}")
    old, new = entries(start), entries("HEAD")
    if tree_id(start, LIST) != tree_id("HEAD", LIST):
        why.append(f"{LIST} changed")
    pats = old + [p for p in new if p not in old]
    hit = (
        set(
            git("diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames", start, "HEAD", "--", *specs(pats)).split(
                "\n"
            )
        )
        - {""}
        if pats
        else set[str]()
    )
    for row in git("diff", "--name-status", "-M", start, "HEAD").splitlines():
        status, *paths = row.split("\t")
        if hit & set(paths):
            why.append(f"listed path ({LIST}): {status} {' -> '.join(paths)}")
    if why:
        return "full", "; ".join(why)
    return (
        "fast",
        f"no path on {LIST} touched, past the full pass at {(passed or '')[:12]} on {branch}",
    )


def tree_id(rev: str, path: str) -> str:
    """PATH's blob id at REV, verified, or `absent`: one id for an unchanged file on any commit."""
    return git("rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"{rev}:{path}", check=False).strip() or "absent"


def gate_config(rev: str) -> str:
    """REV's gate configuration identity: sha256 over each CONFIG file's verified blob id."""
    return hashlib.sha256("\n".join(f"{p} {tree_id(rev, p)}" for p in CONFIG).encode()).hexdigest()


def identity(rev: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    """A full pass's recorded identity besides its head: gate_config, the list's blob id."""
    return {"gate_config": gate_config(rev), "list": tree_id(rev, LIST)}


def record(reason: str, seconds: float) -> None:
    head = git("rev-parse", "HEAD").strip()
    ident = identity(head)
    rec = {
        "tier": "full",
        "head": head,
        "branch": git("symbolic-ref", "-q", "--short", "HEAD", check=False).strip() or None,
        "clean": not git("status", "--porcelain").strip(),
        "gate_config": ident["gate_config"],
        "list": ident["list"],
        "reason": reason,
        "seconds": round(seconds, 1),
        "at": dt.datetime.now(dt.UTC).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"),
    }
    # A note is a commit: it needs the repo's git identity, never one made up here.
    idents = ("GIT_AUTHOR_IDENT", "GIT_COMMITTER_IDENT")
    if not all(ok("-c", "user.useConfigOnly=true", "var", v) for v in idents):
        sys.exit(
            f"octo-feather-gate: full pass of {head[:12]} not recorded: no git identity "
            "(a git note "
            "is a commit): set user.name and user.email, e.g. git config user.name 'NAME' and "
            "git config user.email 'EMAIL' (--global for every repo), or GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL "
            "and GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL; then rerun"
        )
    r = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "notes", f"--ref={NOTES}", "add", "-f", "-m", json.dumps(rec, indent=1), head],  # noqa: S607
        capture_output=True,
        text=True,
        check=False,
    )
    if r.returncode:
        sys.exit(f"octo-feather-gate: full pass of {head[:12]} not recorded: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    sys.stdout.write(f"recorded: full pass of {head[:12]} ({NOTES})\n")


def passed(rev: str) -> int:
    commit = git("rev-parse", "--verify", f"{rev}^{{commit}}").strip()
    note = git("notes", f"--ref={NOTES}", "show", commit, check=False)
    if not note:
        sys.stderr.write(f"octo-feather-gate: no full pass recorded for {commit[:12]}\n")
        return 1
    sys.stdout.write(note)
    return 0


def map_dir() -> Path:
    return (
        Path(git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir").strip())
        / "octo-feather"
        / "fast-map"
    )


def newest_map(head: str) -> dict[str, object] | None:
    best: tuple[int, dict[str, object]] | None = None
    for f in sorted(map_dir().glob("*.json")) if map_dir().is_dir() else []:
        m = json.loads(f.read_text())
        at = m.get("head")
        if not isinstance(at, str) or not ok("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", at, head):
            continue
        n = int(git("rev-list", "--count", f"{at}..{head}"))
        if best is None or n < best[0]:
            best = (n, m)
    return best[1] if best else None


def say(item: str, why: str) -> None:
    sys.stderr.write(f"fast: {item}: {why}\n")


def select() -> None:
    recipes = os.environ.get("GATE_RECIPES", "").split()
    if not recipes:
        sys.exit("octo-feather-gate select: GATE_RECIPES is unset: run it through just fast")
    root = Path(git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel").strip())
    scripts = sorted(p.relative_to(root).as_posix() for p in root.glob("tests/*.sh"))
    native, native_e2e = collected(root)
    items = scripts + native
    ids = [f"{NODE}test_recipe[{r}]" for r in recipes]
    for r in recipes:
        say(r, "static check (every GATE_RECIPES recipe)")
    chosen = choose(root, items, native_e2e)
    ids += [f"{NODE}test_script[{i}]" for i in scripts if i in chosen]
    ids += [i for i in native if i in chosen]
    sys.stderr.write(
        f"fast: selected {len(ids)} of {len(recipes) + len(items)} gate items"
        f" ({len(recipes)} static, {len(chosen)} of {len(items)} test items)\n"
    )
    sys.stdout.write("".join(f"{i}\n" for i in ids))


def collected(root: Path) -> tuple[list[str], set[str]]:
    """The pytest-native test items (each test function outside test_gate.py, its own gate item,
    named by its node id), as pytest itself collects them in the repo's venv, and those of them
    carrying pytest's e2e marker: one collection, whose process writes each item and its marker
    to OCTO_FEATHER_GATE_ITEMS (tests/gate/conftest.py)."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as t:
        listed = Path(t) / "items.json"
        env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.startswith("OCTO_FEATHER_QC_")}
        env["OCTO_FEATHER_GATE_ITEMS"] = str(listed)
        cmd = ["uv", "run", "--locked", "--offline", "--quiet", "pytest", "--collect-only", "-q"]
        cmd += ["-p", "no:cacheprovider", f"--junitxml={os.devnull}", f"--ignore={NODE[:-2]}"]
        p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=root, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)
        if p.returncode not in (0, 5) or (p.returncode == 0 and not listed.is_file()):  # 5: none
            sys.exit(
                f"octo-feather-gate select: pytest's collection exited {p.returncode}"
                f"{'' if p.returncode else ', listing no items'}: "
                f"{(p.stdout + p.stderr).strip()[-2000:]}"
            )
        items: dict[str, dict[str, bool]] = (
            json.loads(listed.read_text()) if listed.is_file() else {}
        )
    return sorted(items), {i for i, m in items.items() if m.get("e2e")}


def source(item: str) -> str:
    """An item's file: a tests/*.sh item is its file; a pytest item's node id leads with it."""
    return item.split("::", 1)[0]


def changed_since(at: str, *pats: str) -> set[str]:
    """Paths changed from AT to the working tree, deletes and untracked ones too; in PATS."""
    files = git("diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames", at, "--", *pats) + git(
        "ls-files", "--others", "--exclude-standard", "--", *pats
    )
    return set(files.split("\n")) - {""}


def is_e2e(root: Path, item: str) -> bool:
    """An item declared end-to-end by its own header line E2E: run by just check only."""
    return E2E in (root / item).read_text(errors="replace").splitlines()


def diff_base(at: str) -> str:
    """The newer of the map head AT and the latest commit of HEAD's history descending from it
    with a recorded full pass on a clean tree (record): what that pass gated needs no selection."""
    best: tuple[int, str] = (int(git("rev-list", "--count", f"{at}..HEAD")), at)
    for rec in records():
        head = rec.get("head")
        if not isinstance(head, str) or rec.get("clean") is not True:
            continue
        if ok("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", at, head) and ok(
            "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", head, "HEAD"
        ):
            best = min(best, (int(git("rev-list", "--count", f"{head}..HEAD")), head))
    if best[1] != at:
        say(
            f"diff base: {best[1][:12]}, the latest recorded full pass on HEAD's history",
            f"newer than the map at {at[:12]}: only changes past it select",
        )
    return best[1]


def default_branch() -> str | None:
    """The default branch's ref, from local refs only (no network): origin/HEAD as the clone or
    `git remote set-head` left it; else, for init.defaultBranch, main and master in turn, origin's
    remote-tracking branch (a CI checkout's), then the local branch."""
    head = git("symbolic-ref", "-q", "refs/remotes/origin/HEAD", check=False).strip()
    if head:
        return head
    names = [git("config", "init.defaultBranch", check=False).strip(), "main", "master"]
    for n in filter(None, names):
        for ref in (f"refs/remotes/origin/{n}", f"refs/heads/{n}"):
            if ok("rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", ref):
                return ref
    return None


def imported(root: Path, test: str, dirs: list[str]) -> set[str]:
    """The in-repo files TEST imports directly (ast, one level, imports anywhere in it), each module
    resolved as pytest's prepend import mode finds it: TEST's own dir first, then DIRS, every dir
    holding a test file or a conftest.py; the configured pythonpath (the kit's scripts/, product
    modules) is left out."""
    try:
        tree = ast.parse((root / test).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, SyntaxError, ValueError):
        return set()
    names = {
        a.name.split(".")[0] for n in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(n, ast.Import) for a in n.names
    }
    names |= {
        n.module.split(".")[0]
        for n in ast.walk(tree)
        if isinstance(n, ast.ImportFrom) and n.module and not n.level
    }
    out: set[str] = set()
    for m in names:
        for d in (str(Path(test).parent), *dirs):
            hit = [
                f for f in (Path(d, f"{m}.py"), Path(d, m, "__init__.py")) if (root / f).is_file()
            ]
            if hit:
                out.add(hit[0].as_posix())
                break
    return out


def main_base() -> tuple[str | None, str]:
    """The default branch's ref (default_branch) and HEAD's merge base with it, empty when there
    is no HEAD, no default branch or no merge base."""
    ref = default_branch() if ok("rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "HEAD") else None
    return ref, git("merge-base", "HEAD", ref, check=False).strip() if ref else ""


def changed_items() -> None:
    """The test items the change adds or changes (--help, changed), as pytest arguments."""
    ref, base = main_base()
    if not base:
        sys.stderr.write("changed: none judged: no default branch or no merge base with it\n")
        return
    files = changed_since(base) - {NODE[:-2]}
    root = Path(git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel").strip())
    listed = lines(git("ls-files", "--cached", "--others", "--exclude-standard"))
    tests = [f for f in listed if re.fullmatch(r"(.*/)?test_[^/]*\.py", f) and f != NODE[:-2]]
    dirs = sorted(
        {str(Path(f).parent) for f in listed if re.fullmatch(r"(.*/)?(test_|conftest)[^/]*\.py", f)}
    )
    files |= {t for t in tests if (root / t).is_file() and imported(root, t, dirs) & files}
    out = [
        f"{NODE}test_script[{f}]" if re.fullmatch(r"tests/[^/]*\.sh", f) else f
        for f in sorted(files)
    ]
    sys.stderr.write(f"changed: {len(out)} files since {base[:12]}, the merge base with {ref}\n")
    sys.stdout.write("".join(f"{i}\n" for i in out))


def beyond_map(at: str, base: str, unreached: list[str]) -> str:
    """Why changed files no recorded coverage reaches send selection to every item: those the
    list names, and those absent at the map head AT (the map cannot know them); else empty."""
    pats = entries("HEAD")
    listed = changed_since(base, *specs(pats)) if pats and unreached else set[str]()
    residual = [f for f in unreached if f in listed]
    unknown = [f for f in unreached if f not in listed and not ok("cat-file", "-e", f"{at}:{f}")]
    why = [f"{', '.join(residual)} on {LIST}"] if residual else []
    why += [f"{', '.join(unknown)} absent at the map head {at[:12]}"] if unknown else []
    return "; ".join(why)


def choose(root: Path, items: list[str], native_e2e: set[str]) -> set[str]:
    e2e = [i for i in items if i in native_e2e or ("::" not in i and is_e2e(root, i))]
    for i in e2e:
        say(i, f"e2e ({'marker' if i in native_e2e else E2E}): skipped, just check runs it")
    items = [i for i in items if i not in e2e]
    m = newest_map(git("rev-parse", "HEAD").strip())
    if m is None:
        say(
            f"all {len(items)} non-e2e test items",
            "no coverage map from HEAD or an ancestor (build one: just fast-map)",
        )
        return set(items)
    at = str(m["head"])
    cover: dict[str, list[str]] = m["items"]  # pyright: ignore[reportAssignmentType]
    failed: list[str] = m.get("not_passed", [])  # pyright: ignore[reportAssignmentType]
    base = diff_base(at)
    since_map = changed_since(at)  # coverage of a test changed since the map is unknown
    moved = {i for i in items if source(i) in since_map}
    changed = changed_since(base) | {source(i) for i in moved}
    reach = {f for fs in cover.values() for f in fs}
    unreached = sorted(changed - reach - {source(i) for i in items + e2e})
    why = beyond_map(at, base, unreached)
    if why:
        say(
            f"all {len(items)} non-e2e test items",
            f"{why}, outside the coverage map's reach (map at {at[:12]})",
        )
        return set(items)
    chosen: set[str] = set()
    for i in items:
        if source(i) in changed:
            say(i, f"changed since the map at {at[:12]}")
        elif i in cover:
            hit = sorted(changed & set(cover[i]))
            if not hit:
                continue
            say(i, f"recorded coverage reaches {', '.join(hit)}")
        elif i in failed:
            say(i, f"did not pass the mapping run at {at[:12]}, so unmapped: always selected")
        else:
            say(i, f"no recorded coverage in the map at {at[:12]}: always selected")
        chosen.add(i)
    for f in unreached:
        say(f, f"changed; no test item's recorded coverage reaches it and {LIST} does not name it")
    say(
        f"{len(items) - len(chosen)} non-e2e test items skipped",
        f"no changed file in their recorded coverage (map at {at[:12]})",
    )
    return chosen


class Tracked:
    """The repo's tracked files, and a measured file's tracked source: itself under the repo
    root, else (a copy of the kit under /tmp) every tracked file sharing its longest path
    suffix; ambiguity over-selects."""

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.root = Path(git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel").strip()).resolve()
        self.files = set(git("ls-files").splitlines())
        self.by_suffix: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
        for t in self.files:
            parts = t.split("/")
            for k in range(len(parts)):
                self.by_suffix.setdefault("/".join(parts[k:]), set()).add(t)

    def source(self, measured: str) -> set[str]:
        p = Path(measured).resolve()
        if p.is_relative_to(self.root):
            rel = p.relative_to(self.root).as_posix()
            return {rel} if rel in self.files else set[str]()
        if "site-packages" in p.parts or p.is_relative_to(Path(sys.base_prefix).resolve()):
            return set[str]()
        parts = p.parts[1:]
        return next(
            (hit for k in range(len(parts)) if (hit := self.by_suffix.get("/".join(parts[k:])))),
            set[str](),
        )


def junit_key(item: str) -> str:
    """ITEM (a tests/*.sh path, or a pytest node id) as outcomes() keys it: a node id
    PATH.py::[CLASS::]NAME as pytest's junit xml names it, classname PATH's module path (and
    .CLASS), then ::NAME."""
    if "::" not in item:
        return item
    path, *rest = item.split("::")
    return ".".join([path.removesuffix(".py").replace("/", "."), *rest[:-1]]) + "::" + rest[-1]


def outcomes(junit: Path) -> dict[str, bool]:
    """Each test item in a pytest junit xml report (junit_key): whether it passed (no failure,
    error, skip)."""
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET  # noqa: PLC0415  # our own pytest run's report

    out: dict[str, bool] = {}
    gate = junit_key(f"{NODE}x").removesuffix("::x")
    for case in ET.parse(junit).iter("testcase"):  # noqa: S314
        name, cls = case.get("name", ""), case.get("classname", "")
        if name.startswith("test_script[") and name.endswith("]"):
            item = name.removeprefix("test_script[").removesuffix("]")
        elif cls != gate:
            item = f"{cls}::{name}"
        else:
            continue
        bad = any(c.tag in ("failure", "error", "skipped") for c in case)
        out[item] = out.get(item, True) and not bad
    return out


def build_map(data: Path, junit: Path) -> None:
    import coverage  # noqa: PLC0415  # only map needs it: the kit's uv venv has it (pyproject.toml)

    if not junit.is_file():
        sys.exit(f"octo-feather-gate map: no junit report at {junit}: which items passed, unknown")
    ran = outcomes(junit)
    tracked = Tracked()
    items: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
    # The pytest items: each data dir named by a node id (GATE_ITEM holds its `/` and `::`).
    native = {f.parent.relative_to(data).as_posix() for f in data.rglob("cov*") if f.is_file()}
    native = {i for i in native if "::" in i}
    scripts = {
        t
        for t in tracked.files
        if t.startswith("tests/") and t.count("/") == 1 and t.endswith(".sh")
    }
    not_passed = sorted(i for i, good in ran.items() if not good and i in scripts)
    not_passed += sorted(i for i in native if ran.get(junit_key(i)) is False)
    for i in sorted(scripts) + sorted(native):
        if not ran.get(junit_key(i)):  # not run, or did not pass: partial coverage, always selected
            continue
        runs = list((data / i).glob("cov*"))
        if not runs:  # not run, or no Python measured: no recorded coverage, so always selected
            continue
        files: set[str] = set()
        for f in runs:
            cd = coverage.CoverageData(basename=str(f))
            cd.read()
            for m in cd.measured_files():
                files |= tracked.source(m)
        items[i] = sorted(files)
    head = git("rev-parse", "HEAD").strip()
    out = map_dir() / f"{head}.json"
    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out.write_text(
        json.dumps({"head": head, "items": items, "not_passed": not_passed}, indent=1) + "\n"
    )
    sys.stdout.write(f"fast-map: {len(items)} test items mapped at {head[:12]}: {out}\n")
    for i in not_passed:
        sys.stdout.write(f"fast-map: {i} did not pass: left out of the map, always selected\n")


MISE_DIRS = ("tracked-configs", "trusted-configs")


class Box(TypedDict):
    """What untouched compares: each watched mise state dir's entries (name: content), the git
    config file's path ("" outside a git repo) and its key/value pairs, branch.<name>.* aside
    (None when absent); and what is this run's: its own TMPDIR (as given and its real path), its
    id (that dir's name), the git common dir ("" outside a git repo)."""

    mise: dict[str, dict[str, str]]
    config: str
    keys: list[list[str]] | None
    run_tmp: list[str]
    run_id: str
    common: str


def entry(p: Path) -> str:
    """One mise state dir entry as content: a link by its target, a file by its bytes' sha256."""
    if p.is_symlink():
        return f"-> {p.readlink()}"
    if p.is_dir():
        return "a directory"
    return f"sha256 {hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]}"


def listing(d: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    p = Path(d)
    return {e.name: entry(e) for e in sorted(p.iterdir())} if p.is_dir() else {}


def config_keys(config: str) -> list[list[str]] | None:
    """CONFIG's key/value pairs as git reads them (`git config --file F --list`), in file order,
    without branch.<name>.* (push -u, a worktree's branch: another lane's, never a run's own
    leak); None when there is no such file."""
    if not config or not Path(config).is_file():
        return None
    out = git("config", "--file", config, "--list", "-z")
    pairs = [kv.partition("\n") for kv in out.split("\0") if kv]
    return [[k, v] for k, _, v in pairs if not re.fullmatch(r"branch\..+\.[^.]+", k)]


def under(target: str, d: str) -> bool:
    return target == d or target.startswith(d.rstrip("/") + "/")


def ours(state: str, content: str | None, was: Box) -> str | None:
    """Where the target of a link in mise state dir STATE, its entry CONTENT (entry(): "-> TARGET"),
    lies if this run made it (a failure), else None: under the run's own TMPDIR, or under a subdir
    of the git common dir's octo-feather/ whose name carries the run's id. Exact attribution:
    nothing else is this run's, dangling or not (another agent's scratch); a file (no target) never
    is."""
    if not content or not content.startswith("-> "):
        return None
    t = os.path.normpath(Path(state) / content.removeprefix("-> "))
    for d in was["run_tmp"]:
        if under(t, d):
            return f"this run's TMPDIR {was['run_tmp'][0]}"
    base = f"{was['common']}/octo-feather"
    if was["common"] and was["run_id"] and under(t, base) and t != base:
        sub = Path(t).relative_to(base).parts[0]
        if was["run_id"] in sub:
            return f"{base}/{sub}, named for this run"
    return None


def keys_changed(was: Box) -> list[str]:
    """The config's key/value pairs added or removed since WAS, branch.<name>.* aside."""
    k0, k1 = was["keys"], config_keys(was["config"])
    if k0 == k1:
        return []
    c0 = Counter(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in k0 or [])
    c1 = Counter(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in k1 or [])
    said = [f"-{x}" for x in sorted((c0 - c1).elements())]
    said += [f"+{x}" for x in sorted((c1 - c0).elements())]
    if not said and (k0 is None) == (k1 is None):
        return []  # the same pairs, another order
    now = "absent" if k1 is None else "present"
    return [f"{was['config']}: changed ({now}): {' '.join(said)}"]


def changed(was: Box) -> tuple[list[str], list[str]]:
    """(failures, notes) since WAS. A mise entry added, removed or changed fails when it is this
    run's (ours: its saved target or its new one), else it is a note: another agent's, such as a
    peer lane's post-merge prune removing its worktree's links meanwhile (#664 director ruling).
    Any config key/value added or removed fails (keys_changed)."""
    out: list[str] = []
    notes: list[str] = []
    for d, before in was["mise"].items():
        after = listing(d)
        for n in sorted(before.keys() | after.keys()):
            b, a = before.get(n), after.get(n)
            if b == a:
                continue
            if a is None:
                what = f"{d}/{n}: removed (was {b})"
            elif b is None:
                what = f"{d}/{n}: added {a}"
            else:
                what = f"{d}/{n}: changed ({b}, now {a})"
            where = ours(d, b, was) or ours(d, a, was)
            if where:
                out.append(f"{what}, under {where}")
            else:
                notes.append(what)
    return out + keys_changed(was), notes


def untouched(action: str, file: Path, mise_state: str, run_tmp: str) -> int:
    """save: FILE holds the caller's mise state (MISE_STATE), this repo's git common dir config's
    keys and RUN_TMP, the run's own TMPDIR. check: read again from the paths FILE names; each
    failure printed, exit 1 on any, else one line naming what was unchanged; notes either way."""
    if action == "save":
        common = git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir", check=False).strip()
        config = str(Path(common) / "config") if common else ""  # "": not in a git repo
        dirs = [str(Path(mise_state) / d) for d in MISE_DIRS] if mise_state else []
        box: Box = {
            "mise": {d: listing(d) for d in dirs},
            "config": config,
            "keys": config_keys(config),
            "run_tmp": list(
                dict.fromkeys(p for p in (run_tmp, os.path.realpath(run_tmp)) if run_tmp)
            ),
            "run_id": Path(run_tmp).name if run_tmp else "",
            "common": common,
        }
        file.write_text(json.dumps(box))
        return 0
    was = cast("Box", json.loads(file.read_text()))
    changes, notes = changed(was)
    for n in notes:
        sys.stderr.write(f"check-tests: not this run's: {n}\n")
    if changes:
        sys.stderr.write(
            "check-tests: FAIL the gate changed the caller's mise state or the repo's git config"
            " (#664):\n" + "".join(f"  {c}\n" for c in changes)
        )
        return 1
    seen = [f"{d} ({len(e)} entries)" for d, e in was["mise"].items()]
    keys = was["keys"]
    held = "absent" if keys is None else f"{len(keys)} keys"
    conf = f"{was['config']} ({held}, branch.* aside)" if was["config"] else "no git repo"
    found = ", ".join([*(seen or ["no mise state dir (mise not on PATH)"]), conf])
    sys.stderr.write(f"check-tests: unchanged by the gate: {found}\n")
    return 0


def main() -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="octo-feather-gate",
        description=__doc__,
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    c = sub.add_parser("checkpoint")
    c.add_argument("start")
    c.add_argument("--full", action="store_true")
    c.add_argument("--no-fast", action="store_true")
    r = sub.add_parser("record")
    r.add_argument("--reason", required=True)
    r.add_argument("--seconds", type=float, required=True)
    p = sub.add_parser("passed")
    p.add_argument("rev", nargs="?", default="HEAD")
    g = sub.add_parser("config")
    g.add_argument("rev", nargs="?", default="HEAD")
    sub.add_parser("select")
    sub.add_parser("changed")
    sub.add_parser("base")
    m = sub.add_parser("map")
    m.add_argument("data", type=Path)
    m.add_argument("--junit", type=Path, required=True)
    u = sub.add_parser("untouched")
    u.add_argument("action", choices=("save", "check"))
    u.add_argument("file", type=Path)
    u.add_argument("--mise-state", default="")
    u.add_argument("--run-tmp", default="")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    if a.cmd == "untouched":
        return untouched(a.action, a.file, a.mise_state, a.run_tmp)
    if a.cmd == "checkpoint":
        tier, why = checkpoint(a.start, full=a.full, fast=not a.no_fast)
        sys.stdout.write(f"{tier}\n{why}\n")
    elif a.cmd == "record":
        record(a.reason, a.seconds)
    elif a.cmd == "passed":
        return passed(a.rev)
    elif a.cmd == "config":
        rev = git("rev-parse", "--verify", f"{a.rev}^{{commit}}").strip()
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(identity(rev)) + "\n")
    elif a.cmd == "select":
        select()
    elif a.cmd == "changed":
        changed_items()
    elif a.cmd == "base":
        ref, base = main_base()
        if not base:
            sys.stderr.write("base: none found: no default branch or no merge base with it\n")
            return 1
        sys.stdout.write(f"{base} {ref}\n")
    else:
        build_map(a.data, a.junit)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
